# Argus Arena. Copy to .env, fill in the blanks, then: docker compose up -d

# The address people open: https://DOMAIN (also gateway.DOMAIN and argus.DOMAIN).
DOMAIN=llm.localhost
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# Where models live, on a fast disk the app (uid 1000) can write. A folder that holds models
# already is used as it is.
MODELS_DIR=./models
# Where the stack's data lives (the database, the indexes, the metrics and logs): an absolute
# folder on the host, one folder in it per service. The installer asks, and makes them.
DATA_DIR=
# Where the engine keeps conversations' caches (Admin -> Settings -> Engine: their size, how long):
# a fast disk, an NVMe; empty: DATA_DIR/kvcache.
KV_CACHE_DIR=
# The first chat model: a Hugging Face repo:quant, or a .gguf in MODELS_DIR. It is
# added (and kept loaded) once its files are in MODELS_DIR. More are added under
# Admin -> Models.
MODEL=unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL
# The default models (MODEL, and the picture, video and speech models) are never
# downloaded on their own: "download" has the app download them once, at its first
# start; empty, an admin does under Admin -> Models -> Default models, or their files
# are copied into MODELS_DIR (the installer offers all three).
DEFAULT_MODELS=

# The features that are on (deploy/features lists every one: what it runs, what it needs). A
# feature not named here runs nothing, and the app leaves it out; installer.sh --with and
# --without change the list. These are the defaults:
COMPOSE_PROFILES=chat-models,knowledge,argus,pictures,video,speech,sandbox,web-search,monitoring,gpu-monitoring,power-limits,meetings,lab,apps,data,decks,media,agents,code-studio

# Secrets. Make each with: openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
DB_PASSWORD=
APP_KEY=
ENGINE_KEY=
# Code Studio's workspaces (the workspaces feature): the key the app drives them with.
WORKSPACES_KEY=
ARGUS_KEY=
# The gateway's master key must start with sk-: echo sk-$(openssl rand -hex 32)
GATEWAY_KEY=

# Optional
# HF_TOKEN=                      for gated Hugging Face models
# ACME_EMAIL=                    real certificates from Let's Encrypt (a public DOMAIN)
# HSTS_SECONDS=                  browsers keep to https for this long (Strict-Transport-Security); empty: a year
#                                with ACME_EMAIL, none with your own CA. With your own CA: 31536000 once every
#                                browser trusts it (a browser that does not could never click past the warning)
# GITLAB_URL=                    the code index: your GitLab and a read-only token
# GITLAB_TOKEN=                  (read_api and read_repository)
# GITLAB_USERNAME=               only when no token can be made: Argus signs in once
# GITLAB_PASSWORD=               with these and makes its own token (a username wins over a token)
# GITLAB_LDAP=                   an LDAP account: empty tries GitLab's own sign-in, then the LDAP ones;
#                                a provider's name (ldapmain) only that one; off: never LDAP
# GITLAB_VERIFY_TLS=false        testing only: accept any certificate from GitLab
# GITHUB_API_URL=                reviews of GitHub pull requests: empty is github.com, a GitHub Enterprise
#                                API (https://github.example.com/api/v3), or off; each person links a token
# GITEA_URL=                     reviews of Gitea pull requests: your Gitea (https://gitea.example.com)
# ARGUS_PACK_LIBRARY_DIR=        built knowledge packs (Admin -> Packs) kept elsewhere than the repository's packs/
# BACKUP_DIR= BACKUP_COPY_DIR= BACKUP_KEEP=14 BACKUP_INCLUDE_LOGS=1 BACKUP_TIME=03:30
#                                scripts/backup.sh: where backups go, a second copy, how many, when
# HTTP_PORT=8080 / HTTPS_PORT=8443  other ports (rootless Podman cannot take 80 and 443)
# DB_HOST= DB_PORT=5432 DB_USER=arena   an external Postgres (16 or newer) instead of the stack's;
# DB_SSL_MODE=require                    leave postgres out (docs/deployment.md, "External Postgres")
# APP_REPLICAS=2                 with scale.yml: several app replicas behind Traefik
# laya (a feature)              Laya, typed decisions on the CPU (the Decide tool, Code Arena's
#                                command check); the app fetches its weights (1.5 GB) into MODELS_DIR/laya
# ENGINE_RAM_PROTECT=40g         RAM protected for the engine under pressure (memory.low, never a limit): the
#                                model's layers and experts in RAM stay there instead of being read from disk again
# browser (a feature)           the browser agent: Chromium in its own container (the chat's Browser tool),
#                                reaching only public sites through the app (Settings -> Tools -> Sites the browser agent may open)
# lean (a feature)              the science lab's proof checker: Lean 4 with Mathlib (an image of about 13 GB, built
#                                with Mathlib's library downloaded from its cache), proofs checked with no network;
#                                LEAN_CACHE_AZURE=1 builds it from the cache's Azure store when cache.mathlib.org is out of reach
# studio (a feature)            the media studio's own models on the GPU: a picture's background taken away, speech in a
#                                voice from a sample, music; the app fetches their weights (11.6 GB) into MODELS_DIR/studio
# vllm (a feature)              the vLLM engine (Admin -> Models, engine vLLM), with VLLM_IMAGE= a vLLM image you
#                                have (docs/multi-gpu-server.md §6) and VLLM_SHM=16gb; fake-gpu.yml runs a fake one
# LLAMACPP_BACKEND=cuda          llama.cpp's GPU backend: cuda, rocm, vulkan, sycl, metal, cpu (rocm.yml for AMD GPUs)
# MEDIA_GPU= EMBED_GPU=          the GPU the picture server runs on (empty: the first), and the embedder (empty: the CPU)
# KVCACHE_DIR=./kvcache          LMCache's disk tier for vLLM models (Admin -> Models, KV tier lmcache): fast NVMe
# LMCACHE_REMOTE=                LMCache's shared store (redis://valkey:6379 with the ha feature)
# LITELLM_REPLICAS=2             with ha.yml: the gateway's replicas, sharing their counts in Valkey
# GPU_POWER_LIMIT_W=             watts per GPU
# CPU_POWER_LIMIT_W=             CPU package watts (Intel)
